quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  25,33,"And they do not bring you a single example, but We bring you the truth and the best explanation (in reply to them)."
  25,34,Those who will be dragged upon their faces towards Hell will be in the worst place and are (now) farthest from the right way.
  25,35,"Indeed, We gave Musa (Moses) the Book, and We made his brother Harun (Aaron) accompany him as a minister (for his assistance)."
  25,36,"Then We said: ‘Go, both of you, to the people who have rejected Our signs.’ Then, We destroyed them utterly."
  25,37,"And the people of Nuh (Noah), We drowned them when they denied the messengers and made them a sign for humankind. And We have prepared for the wrongdoers a painful punishment."
  25,38,"And (We also destroyed) ‘Ad and Thamud, the inhabitants of al-Rass (i.e. the water pit) and many (other) generations between them."
  25,39,"And to each (of them), We gave examples (as warnings), and each (of them) We eradicated with utter destruction."
  25,40,"Indeed, they must have passed by the town (of Sodom), which had been showered with a terrible rain (of stones). Have they not seen it? Yet they did not hope to be resurrected."
  25,41,"And when they see you, they do nothing but make fun of you, (saying): ‘Is this the one whom Allah has sent as a messenger?"
  25,42,"Indeed, he was about to lead us astray from our gods if we had not stood firmly by them. And soon they will realise when they see the punishment who is further astray from the (right) path."
  25,43,Have you seen him who takes his desire as his god? Is it your duty to become a guardian over him?
